#. translators: 1: site URL, 2: PHP version, 3: server API, 4: fixed version
#: includes/class-admin.php:576
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hello,\n"
"\n"
"My website %1$s runs PHP %2$s (%3$s). A security scan says this version may be affected by PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619), the critical PHP vulnerabilities announced on October 21, 2026.\n"
"\n"
"Could you please:\n"
"1. Update PHP for my site to %4$s (or your patched package), or confirm that the fix for both CVEs has already been applied to this server, and\n"
"2. Restart PHP afterwards, and\n"
"3. Until then, consider the temporary protections from PHP's advisory (memory_limit = -1 enforced with php_admin_value, session.upload_progress.enabled = 0, a low post_max_size and max_input_nesting_level, pm.max_requests = 1) in php.ini or the PHP-FPM pool. These only partly protect.\n"
"\n"
"Could you also let me know whether you've seen any signs of these attacks against my site since October 17, 2026?\n"
"\n"
"Thank you!"
msgstr ""

